<gpx version="1.1" creator="Good Shit" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1"><trk><name>Daimon-zaka Cedar Stairway — Daimon-zaka Cedar Stairway</name><desc>Daimon-zaka is a roughly 600 m stone stairway on the Kumano Kodo pilgrimage trail near Nachikatsuura. Tall cedars line the climb, giving the approach to Nachi a wooded setting before the busier shrine area. The selected route covers the stairway itself, about half an hour uphill. Continuing to Kumano Nachi Taisha and Nachi Falls makes a longer visit of roughly two hours; those extensions are not part of this mapped segment. The stone steps can be very slippery when wet.

